	{
		Title = "Doomspire 1.5 Balance Patch Part 1",
		Subtitle = "Featuring changes to Grinders and Monocolourless.",
		Date = "March 15th, 2025",
		Card = "Level Up!",
		["Patch Notes"] = { {
			Text = "Foreword\t\nThis patch is part one of the DS1.5 balance patch, focusing on essential fixes to the game's balance. In two weeks time, the second half of this patch will release focusing on buffing struggling strategies and Doomspire Act 1 as a whole.\n\nRules Change\n\"OnDrawn\" effects now trigger when the card enters the hand for any reason.\nThis affects Infernal Fan (token of Infiltrate the Crowd) and the new grinders tokens, seen below. \n\t\t\nGrinders\nNow Reworked; Too many changes to list cleanly here\t\nGo play with them and have fun!\n\t\t\nThunder Bolt\nNow 6W (+WW); Now destroys cards (from obliterates). Now has fading.\nMonocolourless is able to play a large number of boardwipes. This makes contesting the deck particularly difficult, especially when their removal is diverse (lightning obliterates, lobsters damages, etc). I expect the card will need further nerfs down the line; For now though this change forces monocolourless to interact against destroyimmune cards more easily.\n\nThe following cards are now fading.\nIt has been deeply annoying balancing recursion effects around these cards this past year, and control decks being able to hold these cards in hand has never felt good. This change hopes to remove a niche but toxic interaction from the game.\nLuck o' the Lobsters\nSublime Purity\nMass Epidemic\t\nCelestials of Chaos and Fate.\nEcocide\tNow has fading.\t\nAbsolute Authority\tNow has fading.\t\nDwarvern Meteor\tNow has fading.\t\nThe Shadow Realm\tNow has fading.\t\nLeft Behind (This is a token created by Crisis of Faith.)\nContinued\t(This is a token created by Crisis of Faith.) \n\t\t\nStud\nReverted. Now {W}{W}{W} (+{W})\t\nI told you this was too good when I added it. Sometimes you have to let democracy win... This card is used fairly in a variety of bad decks, but is also exploited and abused very easily by cutthroat players. If there's a way of keeping its cool niche uses without letting monocolourless have trivial access to it, I would take it. Perhaps something for DS1.5 Part2.\n\nDamnatio Memoriae\nStuds and Moonleaks given by it are now fleeting.\t\n\nNeoancient Reappearance\nNow 8{W} (+{W}{W})\nThis card is the backbone of many an interesting strategy, but is too efficient. This change hopes to make it more of an investment to use the card.\n\nDeidre, Timeslayer\nNow rank 6. Now 1500/600 (+300/+200).  Now has overload. Continued ability now grants overload.\nThis card exists to be a powerful answer to creature-light stalling decks. The hope is buffing it allows it to achieve this goal more effectively.\n\nTaizjaaja, Neodragon Omnipotent Burning Hell Demonic Fist\nNow gives cards in the opponent's hand fleeting and inert in all zones (from destroying them outright)\nNever listening to a neodragon player downplay their own deck again on god\n\nMaxr3d\nNow requires 80 cards in graveyard (from 60)\t\n\nBoomie\nIs now considered Boomie after being revealed by Boomie's radar (so subsequent radars will buff it)\nChanged by commisioner request. Boomie is a token of Poklolio.\n\t\t\nLuna Zone\nNew cards and additions!\n\nLosslessFormat\t\nColourless Common\n{W}{W}{W}{Y}{Y}{Y} 600/300\nWhenever you cast a card that costs no studs: Give yourself a copy of it, except it costs {W} and has stealth.\nWith special thanks to Flufflefunz\n\nLonely Specimen\nColourless Rare\n{W}{W}{Y}{Y} 300/500\nWhen this card is cast: A target allied fighter gains 50 Health and Power for each allied fighter in its group.\nWith special thanks to catarompany\n\nthe leepymind\nColourless Rare\n{W}{W}{W}{G}{Y} 600/400\nWhenever this card attacks: Give yourself a fleeting Nascent Stud.\nWith special thanks to leepyhead\n\nreality\nColourless Epic\n{W}{W}{W}{W}{R}{G}{B}{Y} 850/350\nRank 6.\nWhen this card is cast: Select a grouped card in your hand. This card joins its group.\nDuring your end step: Destroy the oldest card in your hand. Give youreslf a non-token fighter card and action card in this card's group.\nWith special thanks to reality\n\nMilk & Cheezyz\nColourless Epic\n{W}{W}{W}{W}{W}{W}{R}{G}{B}{Y} 800/550\nTwice each turn, whenever you cast another epic or legendary fighter: Give yourself a copy of that fighter as a +100/+100 gear.\nWith special thanks to Worst_Omen and Cheezyztherecorder\n\nKilljque and Hypns, Stonemasons\nColourless Legendary\n10{W} 2000/1000\nRank 10.\nWhen this card is cast: Destroy a target allied fighter and a targe tenemy fighter, then all players summon an X/150 Effigy. X is their life.\nWith special thanks to Killjque and Hypns\n\nQlir & DRAGONLADY\t\nRed Common\n{R}{R}{R} 350/350\nWhenever you discard a card: Add a non-Colourless stud to this card's cost. This ability also triggers in your hand.\nWhen this card is cast: It deals X damage to all enemy fighters and gains X Health and Power. X is 150 times the number of colours in its cost.\nWith special thanks to Julez_X\n \nLemonade Glass, Buildaround Connoisseur\tRed Common\n{W}{W}{W}{W}{R}{R}{R} 750/450\nRank 4.\nWhen this card is cast or dies, if your starting deck contains only cards that cost at least {W}{W}{W}: Put a Colourless Stud into your baseplate.\nWith special thanks to Lemonade Glass\n\nAsino\nRed Rare\n{W}{W}{W}{W}{R}{R} 650/650\nWhenever this card attacks and destroys another: Give yourself an {R}{R} 350/350 fighter that's inert in all zones and select 1 effect for it — \n🅐 Whenever this card destroys another: Give yourself an alternate art card, except it's Red. Convert all {G}{B}{Y} in it's cost to {R}.\n🅑 When this card is cast: Select a card in your hand and destroy it. If you do, deal 350 damage to a target fighter.\nWith special thanks to Asino\n\nZero_Expectation\nRed Rare\n{R}{R}{R}{R}{R}{R} 150/150\nLiberate.\nOnce each turn, whenever a card leaves your graveyard: This card gains 200 Health and Power. This ability triggers in all zones.\nWhen this card is cast: Destroy the oldest card in each hand. They become liberated.\nWith special thanks to Asino\n\n0x2991; Dying Butterfly\nRed Legendary\n{W}{R}{R}{R}{R} 800/50\nHaste.\nOverload.\nLevel 1.\nAfter this card attacks: Attach marked to a target fighter. If this card's level 4, it can no longer be countered.\nWhenever an enemy marked fighter dies: This card gains 200 Health and Power and a level. Return it to its hand.\nWith special thanks to 0x2991\n\nAlpha-O & Pier - Intergalactic Rivals\nRed Legendary\n{R}{R}{R}{R}{Y}{Y}{Y}{Y} 800/800\nWhen this card is cast: Give yourself 3 gears —\n• A free +100/+100;\n• A {W}{R}{Y} +0/+300 that grants overload;\n• A {W}{W}{R}{R}{Y}{Y} +250/+250 that draws a card when it attacks and destroys another.\nWith special thanks to RifotheRifle\n\nJustDrewLol\nGreen Uncommon\n{W}{G}{G}{G}{G} 700/400\nOnce each turn, whenever an effect damages or depowers an enemy fighter: All cards in your hand gain 100 Health and Power.\nWith special thanks to JustDrewLol\n\nRagatsu Bandala\nGreen Uncommon\n{W}{G}{G}{Y}{Y} Terrain\nAt the start of your turns: You may select a card in your hand. If you do, put it at the bottom of your deck and draw a card.\nWith special thanks to Rayburn89\n\nXi_nal Fan\nGreen Rare\n{W}{W}{W}{W}{G}{G}{G} 750/100\nWhen this card is cast: Select an unranked fighter card in your hand that costs 6 or fewer total studs. Summon a copy of that card with Flowing Shape attached to it.\nWith special thanks to Ykoimonha1115\n\nThe Rusting and the Missing\nGreen Rare\n{W}{W}{G}{G}{Y}{Y}{Y}{Y} 800/400\nOnce each turn, whenever you cast another allied fighter: Attach a copy of it to this card as a +0/+0 gear.\nOnce each turn, whenever this card attacks and destroys another: All gear on it trigger as though they were cast.\nWith special thanks to Rustedhelmet and MissingInvestigat0r\n\nVarya Esfir\nGreen Epic\n{W}{W}{W}{G}{G}{G}{G}{G}{G} 600/500\nStealth.\nWhenever an effect gives you a card: Shuffle the top card of your graveyard into your deck, then put a copy of this card at the bottom of your graveyard.\nDuring your end step: Put a card from your deck into your baseplate for each copy of this card in your graveyard, then summon all copies of this card from your baseplate.\tWith special thanks to Snubccube\n\nGabytaby\nGreen Epic\n10{G} 400/400\nWhen this card is cast: Select an unranked fighter card in your baseplate with total stud cost 6 or less. Summon 3 copies of it, each with 400 Health and Power.\nWith special thanks to Gabytaby\n\nNi'raya Sinz\nGreen Legendary\n{W}{W}{W}{G}{G}{B}{B}{B}{B} 1200/400\nWhen this card is cast: Put a Vengeful Blessing on the 6th, 7th, 8th, 9th, and 10th slot of your opponent's hand.\nWith special thanks to Sinz\n\nFunzCorp Flagship\nGreen Legendary\n{W}{W}{W}{W}{G}{G}{G}{Y}{Y} Action\nGive yourself a copy of a target fighter.\nGive yourself a copy of a target fighter, except it's a gear with -300/-300 stat bonus.\nGive yourself a copy of a target fighter, except it's an action. Remove {W}{R}{G}{B}{Y} from its cost.\nWith special thanks to Flufflefunz and Rayburn89\n\nDeath Awaits\nBlue Uncommon\n{B}{B}{B} Action\nPursue a career in art.\nWith special thanks to Evilcrafts56\n\nArctrooper99, Blessed Monarch\nBlue Uncommon\n{R}{R}{B}{B} 500/300\nWhen this card is cast: Select 1 effect, or both if you have 4 or more blessings -\n🅐 Give yourself a Blue or Red action card, then destroy the oldest card in your hand.\n🅑 Inject a target fighter that costs 3 or fewer total studs.\nWith special thanks to Arctrooper99\n\nYkoimonha1115\nBlue Uncommon\n{G}{G}{B}{B}{B} 500/600\nOnce each turn, whenever your opponent casts an action: They lose {W} and you gain {W}.\nDuring your end step, if you have 8 or more {W}: Recur 2 allied action cards, except they're fading.\nWith special thanks to Ykoimonha1115\n\nShimmering Coat\nBlue Uncommon\n{W}{W}{W}{B}{B}{B} +0/+0 Gear\nAttach to a target fighter.\n0 charges.\nIf this fighter would take damage, spend a charge to negate it.\nDuring your end step, if this card has 0 charges: It gains a charge.\nWith speical thanks uncreativename123\n\nAbandonmint\tBlue Epic\n{W}{B}{B}{B}{B}{B}{B} 500/500\nWhen this card is cast: Choose Dextrous or Defender and give yourself that gear. If there's an allied fighter with total stats 1500, give yourself both.\nWith special thanks to Flufflefunz\n\nThe Dragon Warden\nBlue Epic\n5{W}5{B} 750/750\nRank 6.\nDuring your end step: Summon Falthier, a 450/450 Dragon.\nOnce each turn, whenever an effect would depower this card: Return a target enemy fighter to its hand.\nWith special thanks to The Dragon Warden\n\nPhilabob's Indephilagability\nYellow Uncommon\n{W}{W}{Y}{Y}{Y}{Y}{Y} 900/300\nWhenever an allied attached fighter attacks: Shuffle a Phractured Philabob into your deck, then draw a card.\nWith special thanks to Philabob\n\nDairing, Sorcer Supreme\nYellow Epic\n{W}{W}{R}{R}{G}{G}{Y}{Y} 800/450\nWhen this card is cast: Your opponent summons a 100/0 Portal.\nWith special thanks to Dairingpoophead"
		} }
