	{
		Title = "Pre-Anniversary Balance Patch Part 1",
		Subtitle = "A GIANT changelog.",
		Date = "July 4th, 2025",
		Card = "Meebozo",
		["Patch Notes"] = { {
			Text = "Democracy Zone\nBy the community, for the community.\nThe following changes have been voted on by the community and aren't cringe enough to object to.\n\nBucketWarriors, Robot Overlord: Effect now only gains {R}{G}{B} instead of {R}{G}{B}{Y}{Y}\t\nCambium Tender: Effect now triggers only once each turn.\nWoW can spam out terrains and repeatedly trigger effects that can drastically change trades or boardstate. - Lid\nThe Roil: Effect no longer gives a fighter from the world of wood.\t\nSame reason as above. - Lid This is the token summoned by 'World of Wood.'\n\nChortling Convert: Now {R}{R}{Y} 200/500 (-{R}, -600/+100). Effect now loses 200 life and gives a smiley family card (from shuffling 6 such cards into deck).\nGiven how powerful Laughing Stock has been throughout several times in its life, the idea of printing one that allowed a ransack to go +2 was terrifying. This is a compromise that still gives high ransack density for the deck when it needs it - Myr\n\nClaudia, Preordained Hero: Effect now draws 2 regardless of if the condition is fulfilled.\t\nCloakedyoshi: Now 650/250 (+150/0)\nCard is a fragile snowballer for 2R3Y, it should get at least a slight healthbuff - Lid\n\nCoderQwerty: Effect now attaches Terrified (from giving the passive outright)\t\nCorporate Marketeer: Can now select 10 cards to generate (from 7)\t\nDiddleShot: Can no longer recur token cards.\t\nEisenhower Dwit: Effect now \"Once each turn. Whenever an allied card dies: Summon a clone of it except it's fading and zombified.\"\"\nEricThePianoGuy: Effect now activates on cast. \t\nChanging the proposed change to be more easily usable. - Lid\n\nFlatFlyer, The Last Aegis: Now 1200/600 (-100/+300); Tokens now buff by 300 of their respective stat (from 200)\t\nflufflefunz: Effect trigger now deals 100 damage to all enemy fighters with the lowest health (from all enemies)\t\nGraalgamer: Effect now triggers only once each turn.\t\nHallow's Treasurer: Effect now deals 150 damage to itself instead of 200\t\nHistor, Blood Warrior: Effect now Selects 2 fighters (from 4 random) to summon, but they are zombified. Now 1500/600 (0/+100).\t\nHomingbeacon: Now 600/600 (-300/-1000)\t\nLavatik: Now 500/500 (+0/+200)\nStatbuffed instead to preserve the cool part of the card. Boardsculpt to get that draw! - Myr\nMalevolent Fanboy: Now 600/100 (-100/-0)\t\nMania: Now rank 5.\t\nMinitoon: No longer inert. Now 300/300 (0/-200)\t\nMonument to Hubris: Inject target fighter effect can now only target allied.\t\nRoxapox: Paints given can now only target allied fighters (from any)\nRayburn, Culture Commander: Now {W}{W}{W}{Y}{Y}{Y} (-{Y})\t\nRhine-XLV: Now requires you destroy a card in hand to give yourself a super doeg punch.\t\nSaltyNope, Cardslinger: Now immune to unlocking card effects.\t\nSatyr Nourisher: Effect now can only target allied fighters.\t\nSchismed Ro-Boy: Now always summons an allied Old Robloxite and an enemy New Robloxite.\t\nSplit Ego: Now also draws a card if there's already 4 colours in your baseplate.\t\nSubZeroExtabyte0: Now triggers when it attacks (from after it attacks)\t\nSunflower_s1: Now {W}{B}{B}{B} (From BBB)\nChanged from polled suggestion. Card is strong and is well-liked, but needed to be nerfed, so adding a colorless cost will make it need slightly more investment. - Lid\n\nThe Absolute Shattering: Now only gives copies of fighters that were originally fighters.\nThis solves a few weird infinites the card had - MYr\n\nThe Caishen: Now costs {Y}{Y}{Y} (-{W}{W}). Now triggers when you've targeted thrice this turn.\nThis is some experimental tech. The effect triggers immediately provided you've targeted thrice this turn; If you've done that before it's cast it'll immediately proc. This gives you a reason to use it as well as letting you turn one proc of it into another by casting a second caishen immediately -Myr\n\nThe Golden Suite: Now {R}{R}{Y}{Y} (-{W})\nThe Leepymind: Nascent Stud given is no longer Fleeting\t\nTherapy Dog: Effect now buffs power by 200 (from 200 health)\t\nThesupernessiiiii: Now 800/100 (-200/0)\t\nTrapped Spirit: Now 400/400 (-100/-100)\t\nThese are tokens given by several Yourei cards.\n\nTone: Now {W}{R}{R}{R} 400/400 (-{R} -0/-100).\t\nXxFreezerFlamesxX: Now 600/400 (-300/0)\t\nInfurnished Cultist: Now 500/150 (0/-50)\t\nxxyourdoomxx: Effect now additionally gives cards in hand overload. Now 1600/1600 (+0/+800)\nCard needed a buff to end the game, but giving cards haste overload was a bit much. - Lid\n\n---O3O---\nAuthoritarian Zone\nFrom Myrmiredon, head of the AGCD, with his intern Lid\t\nThe following changes have been made by the head developer to improve gamefeel.\n\n\n---\nGrexit\nGreen being a somewhat underplayed colour means it's acquired a lot of silly cards which we knew were powerful but chose not to address due to them seeing no play. With the addition of specifically Abiogenesis unit, as well as people finally exploring green, we've decided to trim these cards while also buffing non-generic green cards to enable a wider variety of green decks to see play.\n\nAbiogenesis Unit: Now 200/200 (-0/-300)\t\nAncestral martyr: Now 2500/3000 (+0/+500), Recursion effect now \"During your end step, if there's 3 Green cards in your baseplate: Destroy them and recur this card.\"\nI'm not going to lie I thought it always did this - Myr\n\nMaple Collector: Now {W}{W}{W}{W} 500/400 (+{W}, +0/+100)\nThis change makes it costlier to gen 7G T2 going second using it, hopefully without hurting Continued as a deck. While we know this change was unpopular in CCS, we believe that this will continue to be a problem in the future -Myr\n\nOverseer Wizard:\tNow 600/50 (-200/0)\t\nDecaying Protector: Now gains 100 power from its effect. (from 150). Now 1600/0 (+50/-0)\nHealthbuff is to keep it a gigant proc - Myr\n\ngabytaby: Now selects cards that cost 5 or fewer total studs (from 6)\nThis kills the pa00 interaction but otherwise keeps the card in tact. Some people are worried about this quadgenning (or 8x genning in the case of meebs) but I take the opinion that once you get to 10G you have a wide number of options to then ramp into martyr or similar - Myr\n\nSecrets of Swinburne: Now 9{G} (+{G}{G})\t\nEmporium Salesdevil: Now {W}{G}{G}{G}{G} 300/400 (+{G}{G} -{W}, +0/+100)\nThis stops the mass discard into this deck T1 line that has made Emporium difficult to deal with as of late. - Myr\nHasTheHero: No longer has haste; Gains haste when its effect triggers.\t\n\nAnd with a lot of generic green cards culled, we've provided buffs to various non-generic green cards.\nZanzel's Meddling: Now {G}{G} (-{G})\t\nBloxy Announcer: Now attaches overload to what it targets.\t\nWalyn: Now {G}{G} 700/100 (-{W}{W}, -200/-100)\t\nChaoszeroomega: Now 1000/500 (+100/+100)\nGaius, Champion of Vitality: Now gives 2 green cards per trigger (from 1)\t\nSmoothbrained Catgirl: Now also summons a debased catgirl when its effect destroys itself\t\nMonkeymaster: Monkeys given now cost {G} (from {W})\t\nBrymmy: Now uses gears instead of charges. Now 1500/50 (+0/+50)\nThis means you can attach gears/continueds to it for mass gen, as well as use calirolls or similar to get removal. -Myr\n\nJimmyin1: Now 1200/800 (+0/+400). Now has overload.\t\nPalus Dredger: Now buffs the 3rd card space (From any)\t\nRcouret: Now gives 2 blessings (from 1)\nOriginally this gave a blessing as a fun bonus to its main effect, but people keep complaining this card sucks in blessings. Hopefully it sucks less now in this context - Myr\n\n\n---\nMeeboids\t\nMeeboids have been unacceptably explosive for a while: Terrible unless you get meeboid/meeblings in density T1 in which case you baseplate 6 times come T2 and just win on the spot. These changes hope to make meeboids more consistent but less explosive, while overall playing the same; It costs green studs to ramp now so you can't do it T1, but you need fewer resources to ramp and the deck has slightly better cardflow and stats by default. - Myr\nMeeboid: Now 550/200. Effect now \"Whenever you cast a Meeboid fighter: It gains 100 Health and you gain 50 life.\"\t\nMeebling: Once ever, when there's 3 or more Meeboids in your baseplate: Put a Meeboid into your baseplate. All Meeboids gain 100 Health and Power and you gain 100 life.\t\nMeeboid Cultist: Now {W}{G}{G} 400/400. Effect now \"Inert in play. When this card is cast, if there's 2 allied Meeboids: Put a Meeboid into your baseplate and you gain 100 life.\"\t\nJeptem:\tNow {W}{G}{G}{G} 800/200. Effect now \"Once each turn, whenever you gain life: Put a Meeboid into your baseplate.\"\t\nMeeboid King: Now 600/500. Effect now \"At the start of each turn: All allied meeboids gain 100 Health. You gain 100 life.\"\n\nSummon! Meeboid Titano!: Now has fading.\nTitano Awakened\tNow has overload and fading.\nThis is the token summoned by Summon! Meeboid Titano!. This is so it can actually end the game when cast as it doesn't quite have the stopping power to do so. - Myr\n\nMeebozo: New card! See the Luna Zone for details.\nAs PD2 was happening and we felt meeboids didn't have enough deckslots to give players a reason to play all the meeboids, this card was added as a meeboid payoff to help glue the deck together.\n\n\n---\nBargetown\nThis is Lid's first large change as Myr is not able to devote all his time to balance changes like he used to. Let him know how it feels. - Myr\nRules Change: Smuggle\nSmuggled cards become inert when discarded and have their Red and Green stud costs and card color replaced by Blue and Yellow (Red becomes Blue and Green becomes Yellow.)\nAccording to the poll among other thoughts, smuggling is the main part of the problem for bargetown. Allowing the smuggled cards to gen if summoned will make playing smuggled cards more incentivized.\n\nBargetown Backrooms: Effect now \"When this card is cast: Give yourself a smuggled action card that costs 5 or fewer total studs. Once each turn, whenever you cast a smuggled card: Search your deck for a Bargetown card.\"\nA card that is very poor in bargetown as of now, they need a better motivator to summon smuggled cards other than Guns N' Ammo Shopkeep. - Lid\n\nPre-War Technology: Effect Now: Smuggle 2 cards that cost exactly 6 studs. All smuggled cards in your hand cost {B}{Y} less.\nA worse bowl of greed for smuggling. The deck has had problems involving casting the smuggled cards, so now this card's effect discounts after smuggling. - Lid\n\nBargetown Barista: Now {W}{B}{Y} (+{B}). Stats now 450/300 (+50/+100). Effect now searches instead of gives.\nSeen to be too strong with devious doctor at the start, and overall has great cardgen. - Lid\n\nGuns N Ammo Shopkeep: No longer gains health whenever a card is given.\nA card that's known to be strong in bargetown currently, with the major buffs to the mechanic, it should be nerfed. - Lid. Note that this breaks up the gentlemaniac infinite which is a good plus - Myr\n\nKingmaker's Cohort (Darius, the Kingmaker crystal token. 3rd option.):\nEffect now \"Smuggle the top card of your opponent's graveyard, then remove {W}{B}{Y} from all smuggled cards in your hand. Destroy all choice cards in your hand unless you've casted 6 or more smuggled cards this game.\"\""
		} }
	},
	{
		Title = "Pre-Anniversary Balance Patch Part 2",
		Subtitle = "Why did we make it this big ;~;",
		Date = "July 4th, 2025",
		Card = "Plea for Guidance",
		["Patch Notes"] = { {
			Text = "For additional changes to Meeboids, Bargetown, and Democracy, refer to part 1.\n\nThe following changes aim to make lockspam decks more playable. - Myr\nGato Luz: Now 300/300 (+50/+50). Effect now \"When this card is cast or dies: Unlock a target allied fighter, then lock it for 1 turn. Reveal your opponent's hand.\"\t\nPuffytenter12: Instead of its effect, now lockimmune.\tThis means cards that unlock then lock will unlock it.\nFluffle: Now 6{B} (-{W}{W})\t\nWhitescarf: Instead of its effect, now lockimmune.\n\n\n---\nHyliehaven - Red Dominance: First effect now \"Once each turn, whenever you discard a card: Put a Horrific Blessing on a card in your hand\"\nThanks to its multiple blessings, This card singlehandedly enables multiple BR blessing cards. Blessing decks suffer a severe disparity from drawing this card versus not drawing it. This nerf hops to make the RB blessing deck less explosive. - Myr\n\nEnraged Mob: Now 500/300 (+0/+100). Effect now \"When this card is cast: If you have 3 more blessings, it gains 500 power. Then put a Eldritch Blessing onto the sixth card slot in your hand.\"\nThis prevents some insane turns where get 2 of these out by T2 coupled with 3 blessings. Additionally the powergain lets you cast it from a blessed space for a 500/950\n\nRaging Ransacker: Now 6{R} (+{R}). Effect now \"When this card is cast, if you have 3 or more blessings: Deal 450 damage to a target enemy fighter. When you discard this card: Put an Eldritch Blessing on a card space in your hand.\"\nIn contrast, this card has been unappealing. This buff hopes to give these decks, specifically the monored variant, another potential topend. - Myr\n\n\n---\nExtruded Lady: Now 100/300 (+{W}) \nExtruded Gentleman: Now {W}{W}{W} (+{W})\nThis is a futureproofing change as we expect soon to be released content to turn these cards problematic.\n\n\n---\nDetect Imperfection: Now {W}{W} (-{W})\nDebt to the House: Now {W}{W} (-{W})\t\nRemove all Traces: Now {W}{W} (-{W})\t\nWith domain expansion doing nothing at 2W, we've decided to make similar cards also 2W. It used to be the case that these were 3W to stop monogreen getting easy access to card draw, but between enter the doomspire, abiogenesis, and similar, this just isn't a concern anymore. - Myr\n\n\n---\nControl/topend Buffs\nThese changes aim to give control decks more power without turning them into stall decks, so the game slows down a bit more - Lid\nLando64000:\tAdditionally depowers the target fighter by 400.\n1337: Now OmniImmmune (from a bunch of immunities.) Now 9{G}\niamlogic, ultimate gamer: Effect now deals damage to all other fighters (from all)\nThe Dragon Warden: Now 900/900 (+150/+150)\nGrimclaw's Moonbeam: Depower effect now 400 (from 200)\n\n\n---\nMiscellaneous Changes\t\t\nDelirious Ooze: Now 1000/500 (+300/+500)\nDestruction5033: Now 250/250 (-100/0)\nhealth nerf is a buff due to being a picant again - Lid\n\nDominiusConfabricor: Now 900/200 (+0/50)\nExtraterrestrial Tourist: Now 500/300 (+0/+100)\nGrave Scavenger: Now only gains cogs when Colorless fighters are cast. (From any colorless card). Now requires 2 cogs for its effect.\nThis is an interesting card to play around, but has been exploited recently thanks to several cheap token actions being able to make it store a lot of cogs per turn. - Lid\n\nHistor: Now {R}{Y}{Y} (+{R} -{Y})\nJeeeeesus: Effect no longer makes you unable to cast anything else that turn.\nThis is OOOOOOOOLD cheese prevention - Myr\n\nLewa1267: Now deals its damage to a target enemy fighter instead of any.\nMelvin Hat: Now {B}{B} (-{W}). Effect now \"Put a Green Stud into your baseplate. If you've gained 600 or more life this turn, draw a card.\"\nWhile Lid found this to be too oppressive with Valkyries, I took this opportunity to massively simplify the card as it had acquired a lot of crud over the years. I've lowered the cost as it's a larger nerf than I intended - Myr\n\nParting words: Now {W}{W}{W}{G}{G}{B}{B}{Y}{Y} (-{W})\t\nPits Photographer: Now attaches terrified (from applying terrified)\t\nWhile we debated making the card allied only, I feel it being twosided and mucking your opponent up is an important part of its play patterns. -Myr\n\nPowerstone Tower: Effect now only transfers power when an other fighter attacks (from any)\n\t\nRobloxia Strangled: Now 10{W} (+{W}{W}). Now deals overloaded damage\nThis is to ensure that, once the strangled loop is set up and you're casting it every turn, the game approaches an end quickly with less dead time. -Myr\n\nSirAdurite: Now triggers only thrice each turn (from infinite)\nFound to be a problem in both testing and in main server. - Lid\n\nThe Gentlemaniac: Now triggers only 12 times each turn (from infinite)\nThis is a futureproofing change to prevent outright infinites we expect to appear in DSA2. While we accidentially killed the one running around with the bargetown rework, I want to ensure it doesn't happen again. - Myr\n\nYuki, Champion of Emotion: Effect no longer gives power.\nSmouldering Delonix: Effect now thrice each turn. (from no limit)\nUltra Obliterator: Now destroyimmune.\t\n\n\nYYYGraded: Reworked. Now 800/300 (+0/+200). Effect now \"Whenever this card attacks, if the top card of your opponents graveyard costs 5 or fewer total studs: Obliterate it. This card gains 100 Health and Power.\"\nOfficeSpace, Pits Fanatic\tReworked. Now 350/350 {R}{Y}. Whenever this card is cast or attacks: Summon a 100/0 Cheering Demon with no abilities, except it's inert in all zones.\nRemvolt\tEffect now \"During your end step: Give yourself a fleeting Synthetic Subtrate.\"\nSenator Luckytux: Now triggers if there's 6 or fewer total {W} (from 5)\nThese cards were changed per commissioner request - Myr\n\n\n---O3O---\nOSHA Zone\nMaking your life idiotproof since 1998\t\nQoL and other minor things that have to be noted for the sake of completeness.\n\nIncredibly Helpful and Friendly Devil: Now also prevents the casting of gears.\nCrystal of Heroic Ambition: Now also prevents the casting of gears.\nThis is a token summoned by StaceyD06.\n\nShirozaru: Now also prevents the casting of gears.\t\nCensor-Bot: Now also prevents the casting of gears when you cast a fighter. Now prevents the casting of fighters when you cast a gear.\t\nFlatflyer: Now also prevents the casting of gears.\t\nAeonite Progeny: Now also prevents the casting of gears.\t\nCeasefire: Now also prevents the casting of gears.\nThis is a Peace Term token.\n\nForoth Water Technician: Now also prevents the casting of gears and terrains.\t\nHalf-Time: Now only prevents the cating of actions.\nThis is a token summoned by Call to Arms.\nThese cards have been able to have gears snuck under them since DS' release, which goes against the \"cast anything else\" we're wanting. This fixes it.\n\n\n---\nSteve, the Blazing Flare: Now uses Once Each Turn Tech\tThis means you can trigger its effect, cast an additional copy, then trigger its effect again.\nSoul-Star Chorus Familiar: Now uses OETT\t\nChromafex.mp4, The Meteor : Now uses OETT\t\nVioletVelvet: Now uses OETT\t\n\nGraded: Now properly clarifies effects can't change its effect or passives.\nThis makes the interaction with Sublime Purity and Hyliehaven Red Dominance clearer. This is not a bug, but rather an extreme edge case. sunflower_s1 can do the same thing btw - Myr\n\nStairway to Heaven:\tNow slightly less laggy\t\nBloxburg in Solidarity: Can now only summon unranked cards\nFutureproofing - Myr\n\nLiving World: Now shows what it'll animate.\nSlightly unfinished as it needs to show passives but should be good enough. Say thanks to Hexocus!\n\n\n---O3O---\nLuna Zone\nNew Cards and Additions!\n\n6 cards were added to previous packs as part of Pack Doctor 2.\nBrickseeker\t\nUltimate Power; \nRed Uncommon; \n{R}{R}{R} 150/400.\nInert in play.\nWhen this card is cast: You lose 400 life. Animate your terrain into a fighter.\n\nMeebozo\nUltimate Power; \nGreen Rare;\n{G}{G}{G}{G} 700/300. \nOnce each turn, whenever you gain life: Recur an allied Meeboid card, except it's fading and inert when discarded.\n\nHeated Debate\nLunar Impact;\nBlue Common;\n{W}{B}{B} Action.\nIf you have 3 or more blessings, search your deck for 2 Green cards. Put an Eldritch Blessing on a card in your hand.\n\nPlea for Guidance\nBeckoned Masters;\nBlue Common;\n{B}{B} Action.\nThe most expensive fighter in your deck gains 400 Health and Power. Draw a card.\t\n\nUnleash the Titans!\nUltimate Power;\nBlue Rare;\n11{B} Action. \nRank 11.\nAll players draw 11 cards.\nYou can't cast anything else this turn.\t\n\nTitanwarped Terror\nUltimate Power;\nYellow Rare;\n{W}{W}{W}{Y}{Y} 850/850.\nWhenever you cast a card: Give yourself a card for each colour in its cost, then obliterate the 2 oldest cards in your hand.\n\nDefilation of Grief: Now an uncommon (from rare)\nEmergency Medical Team:\tNow rare (from uncommon)\nThese two changes mean we don't have to print 6 cards to colour balance Necrosyndicates. Much easier that way.\n\nThe following two cards were printed as part of the Rorvik Collaboration.\nHard Cheese\nRorvik Collab;\nRed Uncommon;\n{W}{R}{R}{R}{R} +0/+400;\nAttach to a target fighter.\nWhenever this fighter attacks another fighter: This fighter loses all power until your next end step. If this fighter survives that attack: It deals the power it lost as damage, divided evenly among all enemy fighters.\n\nRorvik Atoll\nRorvik Collab;\nYellow Uncommon;\n{W}{W}{Y}{Y} Terrain;\nAt the start of your turns: Your opponent may choose to summon a Giant Ore. If they don't, you draw a fleeting card."
		} }
