	{
		Title = "Pre-Anniversary Gameplay Changes",
		Subtitle = "Non-balance Changes, fixes and QoL updates.",
		Date = "July 4th, 2025",
		Card = "Brickseeker",
		["Patch Notes"] = { {
			Text = "<b>New Collaboration: Rorvik</b>\nWe've just released a crossover collaboration with the Roblox experience: Rorvik! You can complete a quest in both Rorvik and Blox cards for some free rewards in each game!\nIn addition, we've released two new cards based off the game, you can check them out in the Hallow's Bargains shop!\n\n-----\n<b>History Cores Removal</b>\nWith this update, We have made the decision to remove the history core system involved in unlocking new packs.\nThis system didnt hit the mark of what we wanted to achieve in a form of progression for the game, so we'll be removing it and looking into other options that will work better.\nAny history cores you have can be traded into the Exchange shop for BB.\n\n----\n<b>Doomspire Raid Updates</b>\nNormal modes of all of the Doomspire raids are changed! They now use a prebuilt deck themed around the domain and the Candidate in it, so players can play from any point in time!\nThese raid bosses will now also signal their upcoming random attacks the turn before they cast them, to give you the ability to plan ahead.\nIn addition, we've lowered to requirements to unlock all of the story chapters to just 2 completions per raid boss.\n\n---\n<b>New Feature: History Menu</b>\nThe History menu is where you can read up on the lore of Blox Cards and its cards! You can check it out in the library by talking to Merryswole!\nWe will be slowly updating this menu to add more entries over time.\n\n---\n<b>Major Map Expansion</b>\nDuelshire has seen some upgrades! New parts of the map to explore as well as some familliar names have been added to the map!\n\n---\n<b>QoL Improvements and bug fixes</b>\n- Updated the visuals for cards being castable to be clearer\n- Living World and other Terrain Animators will now display the Terrarian info of your active terrain when hovering over them! We'll be updating this feature a bit in coming updates to cover some additional cases and some missing info (such as passives).\n- New players start with all four starter decks\n- A bunch of bug fixes that would take more space than would likely be visible on here\n\n"
		} }
