	[16] = {
		Title = "Balance Patch: Part 1",
		Subtitle = "Act 2 release balance changes!",
		Date = "December 19th, 2025",
		Card = "Broken Dreams",
		["Patch Notes"] = { {
			Text = "This is part 1 of balance changes; The second part will come out on the 31st due to the main designer suddenly falling dizzy and needing more time. I apologise for people waiting promised changes to their lunas or their cards. Please bear with us, but also I'm deeply grateful for your time and support!\n~Myr\n\nThe following changes have been voted on by the community and aren't cringe enough to object to.\nCothran Lushbeast\nEffect now counts all nonfighter cards (from action or terrain)\t\n\nShard Master\nNow 1800/0 (-500/0)\t\n\nLid, Caster of Growth\nnow 2w2b3g1y (-G, +Y).\nEffect no longer adds a colorless stud to the card's cost.\nIts him, nepotis\n\nThe Roil\nEffect now \"Once each turn, whenever you cast a terrain: Search your deck for a card from the World of Wood, then draw a card.\"\t\n\nFlatfunz\nNow Fading. \nFluffleflyer\nNow Fading.\n(These are the tokens from freaky friday)\n\nDespair Surgery\nNow 6G6Y (+GGYY)\t\n\nZombified Chimera\nNow Zombified.\nFlavour win\n\nLusus Naturae\t\nNow 900/100 (+300/-100)\t\n\nNurokoi\nNow 400/350 (0/-100)\n\nLeTruth\nNow 400/250 (+150/0).\nEffect now activates Twice each turn (from infinite)\n\nOpportunistic Coward\nNow triggers when you have 2 or fewer cards in hand (from 1)\n\nSirSorin\nNow gains 150 Power per trigger (from 100)\nHas a mild syntax change to handle the edgecase when it's depowerimmune or strengthenimmune\n\nDehabilitator\nNow 600/400 (+100/+0).\nEffect now \"Once, when your opponent has 3 or more Nightmare cards in hand: Your opponent draws 7 cards. Add {W} to each card in their hand.\"\n\nPseudosanity\nNow 600/400 (+100/+0).\nEffect now \"Once, when your opponent has 3 or more Nightmare cards in hand: Each allied Nightmare card in play and in your hand gains 300 health and power. Actions buffed this way manifest into fighters.\"\tNotably no longers destroys itself. This change was over what was polled to reduce card text.\nNotably no longer destroys itself. These changes were done over what was polled to reduce card text.\n\nJulez, Seeker of Perfection\nNow 800/400 (+100/0)\t\n\nVacelica\nNow 4w8g (+1W+1G).\n\nSterling\nNow has Overload. \nThis is a token from Vacelica\n\nGrieving World\nNow 5r1g (-1R)\t\n\nJunekept\nNow costs 6B (-B)\t\n\nAncalagon, Sword Critic\nNow costs 2w4r1g1y (-R)\t\n\nBaby Noob\nNascent stud given from effect is now fleeting.\t\n\nAvant Guardian\nNow costs 5B (-B)\t\n\nSomaticMizuSan\nEffect now \"When this card is cast: Select any number of cards in your hand.\nRemove {W}{W}{W}{W} from their cost, then add {R}{G}{B}{Y} to their cost.\"\n\nSmoothBlockModel\nNow 950/800 (+150/+0)\t\n\nReckless Recruiter\nReverted; Now gives 50 Power (from 100)\n\nbadcc\nNow 700/700 (-100/-100).\nEffect now draws the opponent 2 cards. (from 1)\n\nFancyFame\nNow 600/400 (+100/+100)\n\nHyliehaven - Black Nihilism\nNow 900/900\n\nApollo, Fearless\nNow triggers once each turn.\n\nShadow of the Apothicons \n(Red form of Faltzen)\nEffect Now: Whenever this card attacks and destroys another: You lose 250 life. Then if you have 2000 or less life, unlock this card. It gains 200 Health and Power.\n\nDisregardian, PHD in Card Game Balance\nNow costs 1W1G1B1Y (-1W)\nhouse repaired\n\nAuthoritarian Zone\t\nFrom Myrmiredon, head of the AGCD, with the intern Lid\t\nThe following changes have been made to improve game balance.\n\nMag\tNow 450/200 (+100/-150)\t\nMag was buffed during Necrosyndicates as we presumed this wasn't the correct statline for a vanilla 1-drop. This buff was a mistake; Issue being we have cards like glaggling gunman et al that make this a hard buff to revert. We hope this statline provides it a niche compared to all the other 1-drop options without it being overwhelming to fight against on an early board. The goal with 1-drops going forward is they're fine, but want to have weaker statlines and not punish slower decks.\n\nChart the Vecross System\nNow sets the cost of what it searches to {W} (from reducing {W}{W}. Can now select any planet (from fetching at random)\nThis card was kinda bad and also doesn't synergise with DSA2's planets. \n\nLiana Lasher\nNow G 500/0; Now gains 100 life from defender\nThis change gives continued a 1-drop so it can more easily generate studs and set up disregard or lifeless rebirth, \n\nApocryspectres\t\nThe biggest glowup this game's ever seen. \nLook for \"Contumacious Astrobleme,\" a new card.\n\nExtants\t\nExtants are not played as a deck. These changes hope to make them more powerful as a package together. Given we had to tone down actual FTKs and T3 kills, I think we did a dercent job in that regard.\nExtant Titanboa\nNow costs {Y} (from {R})\nBeing able to convert studs you have into off-colour studs enables the deck to fix for colours it doesn't have access to.\n\nExtant Smilodon\nNow costs {R} (from {G})\n\nExtant Anomalocaris\t\nNow costs {G} (From {B})\n\nExtant Archaeopteryx\nNow costs {B} (From {Y}); Now summons an X*100/X*100 Offspring instead of X 100/100 Offsprings\nWhen your extant deathcount is at 12 or more, being flooded with offsprings can end the combo and just isn't useful anymore. This change keeps the card useful at high extant deathcounts when you're comboing off.\n\nResin Amalgamation\t\nReworked. Now {R}{R}{G}{G}{B}{B}{Y}{Y} 1000/800. Rank 6.\nWhenever you cast another Extant fighter: Destroy it. Give yourself a Nascent Stud.\nThis card is a proper reward for playing lots of extants, making them all free and allowing you to instantly proc their effects. You can usually OTK the opponent on the spot with enough resources after casting this; But can you survive and get rainbow long enough to?\n\nSomething Evil Will Happen\tNow 3W (-WW)\n\nInfurnace\nEffect Now destroys 2 Hellish infurnitures in your baseplate. (from 2 green cards)\t\n\nDairing, Master of Chairs\nChair giving effect now only activates when the card attacks. (from cast & attacks)\t\nOne of the more oppressive cards of GBY, capable of snowballing by giving you low cost disposable haste fighters.\n\nShadoward12\nEffect now only activates thrice per turn. (from infinite)\t\nA hit to some cheesy terrain strategies given how easy it can be to spam terrains if done properly, also futureproofing.\n\nNoob Gunner\nNo longer summons ranked cards\nThis card is known for being extremely oppressive early, easily helping a noob deck snowball into a wider board with good stats, and setting up for coeptus.\nIt likely will be eating a nerf on the 31st; But for now, it stops you summoning a new DSA2 glad with immense cheese.\n\nStunderworld Luminary\nNow WBBBB, now makes its target fading, now locks its target for 1 turn.\nStops the double removal strat. This card was commed to hose recursion and so the fading is added to keep that part alive.\n\nUnworld\t\nNow triggers for a player after they cast a card (from start of turn)\nThis lets you play a single card which if a powerbuff still lets you do it.\n\nBrometheus, Haunted\tNow 1w2g2y(+1W). Now inert in play.\t\n\n"
		} }
	},
