	[19] = {
		Title = "Pre-DTT Balance Patch",
		Subtitle = "Big balance patch! 1-drops, stall and burst gen weakened, as well as some buffs.",
		Date = "March 22nd 2026",
		Card = "Glint of Perception",
		["Patch Notes"] = {
			{
				Text = "<b>Democracy Zone</b><br />By the community, for the community.<br /><i>The following changes have been voted on by the community and aren't cringe enough to object to.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Forothian Immigrant</b><br />A option now summons a 450/450 with no effect; B option now gives 2 eldritch blessings (from 1); C option now \"Deal 150 damage to all fighters. Destroy your opponent's terrain.\"<br /><i>General buff to all 3 Forothian Immigrant options as all are currently very lacking for their cost. Slight shuffling around of effects to attempt to reduce word count and further properly balance the options.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Sentruko and Studimi</b><br />No longer has haste. Now 700/700 (+150/+150)<br /><i>\nhaving a conditional haste made the card awkward to balance as the red mode wants the card to live, which made the base card really bad to play as a 3R3G 550/550 is not good. stats buffed in exchange of losing haste hoping turn decay makes it killable enough and can maybe still get a proc in</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Humorous </b><br />Now triggers when it attacks and destroys (from destroys)<br /><i>After this card got its lock on colorless fighter target removed its been a major pain and extremely clunky to trade with. Making it on attack destroy to fix self target potency + stop it from just completely deleting certain matchups.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>EricThePianoGuy</b><br />Now triggers on death (from when cast); Now WRBY (+W -B)<br /><i>Partial revert to EricThePianoGuy as currently it being On Cast makes it incredibly volatile and lets the user effectively automatically win early with no means of interaction in 1 card. With a minor cost change as previous cost was clunky while it was ondeath.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>1nicopatty</b><br />Now targetimmune. Now 1700/100 (+0/+50)<br /><i>This card has caused too many issues across a wide variety of decks ranging from Ninjas to Blue Gigants. It has put up exceptional tournament performance, and is generally a widely hated and unfun card. This nerf aims to keep the card playable for niche use cases, but kill it's wide variety of problematic 2 card combos, like attaching Wrath, swapping with theawsomist, or targetting with Froot Ninja.  BHOP chain complete.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Unc, the Consultant</b><br />Now {W}{Y}{Y}{Y} 500/400 (-{W}, -0/-100)<br /><i></i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Snowskateer</b><br />Now 100/350 (-150/-0)<br /><i>Less health means that the card is cleanly answered by Langz or Nicopatty.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Noob Golem</b><br />Now 800/300 (-0/-100)<br /><i>This card has always been a very extreme part of noobs' earlygame, being able to easily disrupt any early plays t2 that may have destroyed a noob. This card on top of its great disruption has a great body which helps the deck keep board. This card being able to disrupt such plays early and have a large body makes it pretty overpowered in noob decks.\n\nLowering its power should help with it being too disruptive early as it now misses notable 400 health benchmarks which can help people disrupt noobs easier without having their fighters instantly killed. The alt change is just that slight bit harsher due to its durability also being a large factor in its strength.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Javionese Immigrant</b><br />A option now a 300/600<br /><i></i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Quality with Quantity</b><br />No longer dextrous<br /><i></i>"
