			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Authoritarian Zone</b><br />From Myrmiredon, head of the AGCD, with the intern Lid<br /><i>The following changes have been made by the ACGD</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Groups</b><br />Reworks/changes to underperforming groups.<br /><i></i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Orinthians</b><br /><br /><i>(Surely the seventh rework will get us there)</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Mindbreak</b><br />Now has an effect: Whenever this card is returned, all mindbroken fighters in hand and field gain 50 health and power. (Mindbreak applies before return on the fighters in question)<br /><i>Mindbreak as a mechanic has only been used for a trigger for deportation depot and ghashendex. It itself doesn't do anything and doesn't help with orinthians' core issues of lacking stats and the inherent disadvantage of self returning. A llittle statbuff helping benefit the returnspam of allied fighters should help it and make the deck more satisfying to play as a whole.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Orinthian actions (strategems)</b><br />All now mindbreak the target fighter.<br /><i>Goes with the changes to mindbreak, these actions now apply mindbreak to make the mechanic more relevant and spreadable across fighters..</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Orinthian Force: Secret Guard</b><br />Effect now:When this card is returned to your hand: A target enemy fighter loses 200 power. You gain 200 life.<br /><i>A complete rework to the card due to how strong it was as an engine, it played weirdly when it was fleeting, and removing the fleeting led to strategies that allowed the orinthian user to completely clear out their deck in 10 turns due to the amount of searches of the orinthian actions there was. This was reworked into something that impacted the board instead, as orinthian soldier already had the card draw when returned, and searching the orinthian actions one after another was deemed too strong.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Orinthian Force: Pilot</b><br />No longer targetimmune. Effect now targets another fighter (from any)<br /><i>Helps with convenience with using the other cards (mainly falcon) and removes an immunity that made dealing with the card a pain (sometimes on both sides)</i>"
			},
