	[24] = {
		Title = "Demon Wars Preparation Patch",
		Subtitle = "A small follow-up of balance changes to prepare for Demon Wars.",
		Date = "August 21st 2026",
		Card = "Reprieve",
		["Patch Notes"] = {
			{
				Text = "<b>Authoritarian Zone</b><br />From Myrmiredon, head of the AGCD, with the intern Lid<br /><i>The following changes have been made by the ACGD</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Minor Dwarf changes</b><br /><br /><i>Slight changes to make the group flow slightly better.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Sentry Alpha: \"DwarfJudge.gif\"\n(Blue Sentry)</b><br />Reworked.Effect now: Whenever an allied Dwarf dies: Draw a card.<br /><i>This sentry is pretty mediocre and while it can be sometimes be useful, is a lot more situational than the rest. This is changed to be draw on a dwarf death to help with Dwarves' cardgen issues.\n(did you know all of the construct actions used to draw, this made them too good at cardflow)</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Dwarvern Pilot</b><br />Now {R}{B}{B}{Y}{Y} (-{W})Effect Now:When this card is cast: Search your deck for a Dwarf card and a Construct card, except they are inert when discarded. Search your deck for Chromafex if you've discarded 5 or more cards this turn. <br /><i>A card that is odd to play in dwarves, and is rough to play with the dwarf starters they search due to the colorless cost. Removing the colorless cost and making it search the construct without needing discards will help it be easier for Dwarves to sustain cardgen unless they want to all-in into chromafex.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>(small) Multicolor buffs</b><br /><br /><i>Fun stuff to prepare for Demon Wars</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Necroforensic Researcher</b><br />Now seances a card that has died this game when it attacks. Now {W}{B}{B}{Y} (+{W})<br /><i>Adding part of its old effect to make it function more smoothly within nefoco.\n</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Astral Faith Zealot</b><br />Endstep effect now buffs by 100/100 (from 50/50)<br /><i>Slightly underwhelming card, while it can make injected cards pass notable benchmarks, it has trouble making a massive impact on the board.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Robloxian Immigrant 1st crystal\n(Robloxian Trowel)</b><br />Now increases the health of all allies by 250 health (from 200)<br /><i>This action is slightly outclassed by nostalgia knights green option and the body of the card doesn't fully make up for it either.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Katharan Immigrants 1st crystal\n(Katharan Charge Blade)</b><br />Now deals 500 damage (from 400)<br /><i>Insert joke about Bloodspilled. This option didn't hit notable benchmarks many other cards (including ones at similar or even lower prices) can.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Katharan Immigrants 2nd crystal\n(Katharan Totem)</b><br />Now 600/300 (0/+100)<br /><i>Going with the theme of each immigrant getting decent fighter options, this one had low power that made this option underwhelming.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Frank East</b><br />Endstep effect now attaches a gear regardless if it has moved one or not.<br /><i></i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>skydec808 Protector of RGB</b><br />Now costs {W}{W}{W}{R}{R}{G}{G}{G}{B}{B} (-{W})<br /><i>Weirdly positioned card that can have good benefits but its high colorless keeps it from flowing well with a lot of other fighters.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>A Candid Conversation</b><br />Now costs {W}{W}{R}{R}{B}{B}{B} (-{R})<br /><i>Was a bit risky to house implode this card due to being big opponent interaction, so instead, a colored cost was removed for it to be used easier, whether it be RB or tricolor.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Rangemelude</b><br />Level 7 death effect now also unlocks the summoned fighter.<br /><i>For the tempo this RBY card can go, and the many synergies around it, the payoff to getting to level 7 is a bit underwhelming. </i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Nooooooo</b><br />Endstep effect no longer requires there to be no enemy fighters to activate.<br /><i>Weirdly placed card in RBY, while RBY can go heavily into zombified cards, this card's effect is very wonky to work with, so needed to be changed to play better.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Parting words</b><br />Now {W}{W}{W}{G}{G}{G}{B}{B}{B}{Y}{Y}{Y} (+{G}{B}{Y})Effect now:Effect: Fading. Obliterate all fighters on the left side of the board. Give yourself a zombified copy of each obliterated card with all {R} in their cost converted to {W}.<br /><i>Parting words is a very weird card to play out, so outfitting it to be more of a winmore or control tool that affects enemy fighters only could be a fun way to make the card play better.</i>"
			},
			{ Text = "<b>Misc Changes</b><br />Other ACGD changes.<br /><i></i>" },
			{
				Text = "<b>Qlir & DRAGONLADY</b><br />Effect Now:Effect: Whenever you discard a card: Add a non-red coloured stud to this card's cost. This ability also triggers in your hand.When this card is cast: It deals X damage to all enemy fighters and this card gains X Health and Power. X is 150 times the number of non-red colours in its cost. <br /><i>This change and the two below are to make the card play better and be more consistent, as there were many cases where you would get basically nothing more out of the effect since it added its own color.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Varis & Thromton</b><br />Effect Now:Whenever you discard a card, if this card's in your hand: Add a non-green coloured stud to its cost.When this card is cast: A target fighter loses X Power and this card gains X Health and Power. X is 150 times the number of non-green colours in its cost. <br /><i>Effect Rework requested by commissioner</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Chidera & Chiroco</b><br />Effect Now:Whenever you discard a card, if this card is in play or your hand: Add a non-yellow coloured stud to this card's cost. When this card is cast: For each non-Yellow colour in its cost, Give yourself a Nascent Stud and this card gains 150 Health and Power <br /><i></i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Pillows, Mass Reformer</b><br />Now 700/300 (0/+50)<br /><i>Slight buff to the card to make it a more reasonably statted option for some give-based group decks.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Dairing, Lorekeeper of Strife</b><br />Now rank 5. (from no rank)<br /><i>had a habit of being summoned t1-t2 and snowballing off of whatever it summoned + being a potent colorless genner.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Rageborne Pulverizer</b><br />Now 500/500 (-50/-50)<br /><i>minus fifty. This card is a real pain and is very capable of easily snowballing games on its own, so nerfing it down to an easier benchmark for people to interact with it easier will help some people fight against it.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>RoyStanford</b><br />Now 600/600 (+50/+50)<br /><i>plus fifty</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>David Crissbach</b><br />Stats Now 400/400 (+200/+200)<br /><i>Card with very poor base stats, while you would mostly use this card for its rather funny effect, the base stats of the card also it down a bit. </i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Alpha Brick's Delirium</b><br />No longer attaches terrains with Terror passive.<br /><i>Removes some interactions where it had a decent chance of attaching a Winter Horrorland Terror, which could cause the card to be easily animated it and deleted from existence.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>papasmurf</b><br />Now only summons drakobloxxers from baseplate. (from baseplate and graveyard)<br /><i>Was too easily able to summon a full board of drakobloxxers by playing the game.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>altiked</b><br />Now 450/250 (-50/-50). Cast effect now applies to all altiks (from all other altiks). (Altik is still 500/300 after effect at base)<br /><i>Requested by Commissioner</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Final Revels</b><br />No longer has Unique.<br /><i>You can no longer use ellernate to delete the opponent hand with this card.\nalso this card is cool try it out</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Defensive Digging</b><br />No longer can summon ranked cards that cost 4 or less studs with its first effect (from no restriction)<br /><i>I was stupid and was supposed to put it in the previous patch notes but then I didn't so it wasn't coded in. - Lid</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Raging Ransacker</b><br />No longer blesses a card in your hand when discarded.<br /><i>Intended to be nerfed last patch. Good card with an insanely good ondiscard effect in a deck all about reaching certain blessing benchmarks that allow red blessings to get its very strong effects earlier than intended. Plus its just amazing value to get such an effect ondiscard.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>CRiMP Crew</b><br />Reworked. now 2C7G, 600/700.When this card is cast a target fighter gains continued, deal 500 damage to it.<br /><i>haha 67 - rayburn67\nRequested by Commissioner</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Sprinter (previously known as Carnation)</b><br />Effect now Twice per turn. (from Once per turn)<br /><i>The effect was capped to once per turn due to some notable exploits with Awesome Weapon Guys along with a few other fleeting synergies. The cap now has been increased to twice a turn for a bit more buildarounds.</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>Infinite Wishes</b><br />Reworked. Effect Now:Fading.All allied fighters gain 150 health. You gain 150 life. Give yourself a copy of this card except it costs 1G more. <br /><i>Infinite wishes was a very centralizing ramp card that was a very easy sink for any green deck, as it was an easy way to gain baseplate and was easy to cast again and again due to its own effect, making it the best studsink for a lot of monogreen decks, not just ramp. This rework is to keep it in line with the other infinite actions in terms of its effect not feeding into itself. (while also being the inverse of infinite flames)</i>"
			},
			{
				Text = "<b>OSHA Zone</b><br />QoL and other boring stuff<br /><i></i>"
			},
