	[24] = {
		Title = "Post-Demon Wars Snipe Patch",
		Subtitle = "Minor adjustments to help with lag and other anomalies",
		Date = "September 6th 2026",
		Card = "Lagswitch",
		["Patch Notes"] = { {
			Text = "CARD CHANGES\n\nBrixzee! and Uranium (Ft. Red Brixzee!)\nNow reworked.\n{W}{W}{W} 150/350\nWhenever you discard a card: Add {B} to this card’s cost.\nWhen this card dies: Search your deck for a fighter with the same total stud cost as it. If it costs 6 or more total studs, that card gains 200 Health and Power.\n(Myr was overworked getting Demon Wars out and thusly this latest batch of lunas didn't have the same level of oversight they're supposed to have. My apologies.)\n\nRules Change\nSuspension and Division preserves \"Once\" and \"Once Each\" restrictions across its clones.\n(If you divide a card that's already triggered it, you don't get to trigger it again. While initially a cool tech, this has been causing repeated problems and was preventing us from printing division effects in any serious capacity. This change was already in the game but not announced.)\n\nWilliam the Conqueror\nEffect now ignores handsize, actions now have stealth\n(Kicking myself spending so much time making Herrus evilproof only to get hit with the most basic Xenotrent tech sobbing)\n\nAdded the Conquerors Logo to specifically demons in DWA1\n\nFixed Empty Office (Token from the Cataclysm) softlocking the game \n\nON LAG\nThis patch contains a few backend fixes to the leaderboards as well as an experimental automatic 10 hour server reset in public servers that should deal with the lag problems people have been complaining about; This timer isn't present in private servers.\nWe'll be continuing to monitor the situation and making incremental improvements.\nIf you detect any other lag spikes or have any concerns, let us know in the community server.\n\nA followup patch will be happening next week as we ensure Demon Wars is behaving properly, likely containing multiple balance adjustments across the rest of the card sandbox.\nThank you for considering why people feel such a need to subjugate others in BLOX CARDS.\n\n\t\t\t"
		} }
	},
	[25] = {
		Title = "Post-Demon Wars Balance Patch",
		Subtitle = "Featuring changes to monocolourless, stall, celestials, and a rule change!",
		Date = "September 20th 2026",
		Card = "Broken Dreams",
		["Patch Notes"] = { {
			Text = "Rules Change: Oversummoning\t\nWhen you have a full board, you may now obliterate the leftmost fighter to make space.\t\nHere at blox cards, we love depower effects for allowing interaction against specifically stats while still giving people value from on end effects or similar, but we're not allowed to print them because of \"softlock\" strategies which print hardcore stall. This change has been touted for a while, and hopes to remove a universally unfun and problematic aspect of the game. Later on you'll see cards that likely encourage you to oversummon...\n\nRukatuKDH\nNow 500/500. (-1500/-1500)\nEffect Now \"When this card is cast, if you have 7500 or more life: Quadruple this card's stats.\"\nAn alternative to the polled change which is overall a buff: Does funny things with return effects.\n\nSurvivor's Camp\t\nEffect now deals all damage to all allied fighters (from all fighters).\t\n\nApocryphic Seeker\nEffect changed to different ordering.\nEffect now \"Give yourself 3 green fighter cards. Put a doomed blessing onto 3 cards in your hand.\"\nThis makes the downside more relevant.\n\nGreenbelt Surveyor\nNow {W}{W}{W}{W} (+{W})\nGoing forward any starter that generates multiple studs likely wants to be 4{W}\n\nSpiteful Apocryphantom\t\nNow 250/0 (350/100 after effect) (-250/0)\t\n\nThe V in Forevermore\nNow only activates during your turns (from any turn); Now 800/100\nForcing your turn cleans up some weird interactions. Between Ophelia, Pillows and this, we have a few similar cards running around. This change hopes to diversify it compared to its contemporaries by still keeping its powerful cardflow at the cost of being useless in direct combat.\n\nBlue/Red actions (colloquially called the Lunar Pool)\nIncreased the number of cards which can be randomly obtained from this pool\tToo many cards to list here; Most RB actions from Necrosyndicates and onwards are now in the lunar pool and can be randomadded by the likes of Wer8888.\n\t\t\nShirozaru\nNow {W}{W}{W}{W}{B}{B}{B}{B}{B}{G}{G}{G}{G}{G} (-{W})\t\n\nDamnatio Memoriae\nNow unranked. \nNow 4{W} (+{W}{W}). \nEffect now \"At the start of your turns, if your starting deck has only Colourless cards in it: You gain {W}. Give yourself a moonleak and a nascent stud.\"\tThis card is awkward in technician decks and monocolourless more generally. This change hopes to enable the enabler for these decks without creating a morbillion stall decks from it.\n\nEmergency Repairs\nNo longer ranked. \n\nPedronomy\nEffect now \"Once, whenever you cast another fighter: It joins Pedromony's group. Both players gain {W}[W}. Whenever a fighter in Pedromony's group attacks: Both players gain 300 life and a nascent stud.\"\nPedromony is a funny cycle of cards. This hopes to improve gameplay for people playing them while still retaining its use in monocolourless and sinisters; The nascent stud lets you go into Unlicensed Pedromony or similar.\n\nVulcanalia, holy city\nNow immune to destruction card effects.\t\nWe were initially scared this card would break the game and gave it no immunities, a general principle behind terrains where they should be easily answerable. With the increased amount of enemy-summoning terrains and terrain bouncing, these threats are less serious. Going forward, we will be printing destruction immunity only on cards that are necessary for its function (such as brick's delirium)\n\nWhalesong Shield\nNow obliterates (from destroying)\t\n\nNevermore\nNow 10R (-{W}{W})\nThis card was designed during an era of immense caution towards cards that win the game without interacting with the board. You have better and more efficient ways of ending the game if you're on that type of deck, and this has decent stallbreaking applications.\n\t\t\nMeta Girl\nReworked.\nNow {W}{W}{W}{R}{R} 600/500\nThis card is immune to destruction card effects. When this card is cast: Reveal your opponent's hand and select an action card in it. Destroy that card.\nThis card has been reworked to be a better antistall option, able to rip boardwipes out of the opponent's hand as well as being immune to a lot of them. Note that it can't rip terrain or gears.\n\nAudi80\nReworked. \nNow {W}{W}{W}{B}{B}{B}{B}{B}{B}{B} 1350/350. \nDextrous. Once each turn, as your opponent casts an action: Negate its effect.\nAnother antistall option, for much the same reason.\n\nAnimites\nReworked. \nNow {W} 7{Y} 700/800.\nWhen this card is cast or after it attacks: It spirals. For each gear on this card, each player destroys a nonfighter card in their hand and searches for a fighter card.\nAnother antistall option for people to tech into. I probably should've printed a tricolour one of these but that's what DW is for isn't it\n\nFraying Pipes\nNow RR (-W\nSay it with me kids; Another antistall option\n\nJackSmirking\nNow WWYY 300/200 (-WY). Effect Now empowers by +50/+50 and debuffs by -50/-50 (From 100 each). \nOne of the most terrifying cards in the game's history returns with the aim of buffing tricolour. Be responsible with it!\n\nGlaecium\nNow 700/0 (400/300 after effect) (0/-100). Now costs {W}{G}{G} (-{W})\nTwo of the most terrifying cards in the game's history returns with the aim of buffing tricolour. Be responsible with it!\n\nCelestials of Time and Space\nNow lets you choose from both modes (instead of forcing 5500 life payment if you can afford it)\t\n\nCelestials of Chaos and Fate\nReworked. \nBBBGGG Action\nYou gain 1000 life.\nA target fighter gains haste.\nReturn it to its hand. \nGive yourself a Celestial Remnant. \nFor each Celestial card in your hand, deal 100 damage to all fighters.\t\nThese two celestial changes aim to improve pure celestials at the expense of generic BG stallslop.\n\nA War of All Against All\nNow {W}{W}{W}{W}{G}{G}{G} (+{W})\nWhile a middle wipe like this has positive effects on the metagame when there's aggro decks running around, this one was more efficient than I thought it would be.\n\nThe Robloxian Overlay\nNow Rank 8 (from 6)\t\nQueue change; This deck was bad but it was good enough and fast enough to be a viable queue grinding deck, causing a miserable experience. These types of cards are good for the game to exist but not healthy if they're competitively viable.\n\nFaltzen\t\nNow 2000/300 (+0/+300)\t\n\nMaplestick\t\nEffect now only applies to each allied fighter with the lowest power (from any). Now triggers only once each turn.\t\nMostly a QoL change that prevents a lot of needless decision making.\n\nCreptiqal\nNow gives {B}{Y} per trigger (-{R})\t\n\nZerax the Untameable\nEffect now \"When this card is cast: Your opponent loses 700 life. You gain 700 life.\"\t\nThis enables the card to work with Nova.\n\nDissing Dissident\nNow {R}{R}{R} 500/350 (+{R}, +150), now destroys 3 cards when cast (from 2)\t\nThis card suffers from a bit of design degeneracy; It's meant to be a card that rewards you ransacking, yet players cast it T1 and drawing cards off it, doing nothing when its condition goes offline. This change hopefully forces you to play with the card's intended gameplay. While we are looking at Clansman o' the Heights, it supports a lot of powerful and interesting decks (such as the tricolour survivor Search the City), and thus do not want to nerf it at this time.\n\nV_yriss\t\nNow a state trigger (from when cast)\t\n\nBrixzee! and Uranium (Ft. Red Brixzee!)\nNow a 200/400 (+50/+50)\nChanged per commissioner request\n\nPits Photographer\nNow 300/600 (-100)\nWith the advent of oversummoning, we know that CF-esque decks are going to receive large unintended buffs. With the general opinion that monoyellow is overall not good right now, we've decided to let this card be more easily crashed into while still allowing it to achieve its gameplan. These types of decks are something we will be watching closely as we move into DWA2.\n\n\t\t\t\t\nCriticism Against Inaction, The Lunar Arch, Great Injustice City\nImproved behaviour when not a terrain in the terrain zone\nIn case you cocoawarrior or vulcanalia it.\n\t\t\n\t\t\nThank you for being here in this wonderful game and community.\n\n\t\t\t"
		} }
	},
